WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:01.842
Hi, this is Fernando.

2
00:00:01.842 --> 00:00:05.514
If you have never used AWS, this video is for you.

3
00:00:05.514 --> 00:00:06.909
The idea is simple.

4
00:00:06.909 --> 00:00:10.874
You learn by testing, not by memorizing service names.

5
00:00:10.874 --> 00:00:13.224
AI sits next to you, as a tutor.

6
00:00:13.224 --> 00:00:16.382
But you are the one who writes and decides.

7
00:00:17.400 --> 00:00:18.872
Here's how it works.

8
00:00:18.872 --> 00:00:21.963
First, a real question, in your own words.

9
00:00:21.963 --> 00:00:23.361
Then, a small test.

10
00:00:23.361 --> 00:00:25.422
Next, you keep the evidence:

11
00:00:25.422 --> 00:00:28.071
what you expected and what happened.

12
00:00:28.071 --> 00:00:30.941
Finally, you write an article about it.

13
00:00:30.941 --> 00:00:33.443
Each mission takes about one hour.

14
00:00:34.467 --> 00:00:36.298
There are three missions.

15
00:00:36.298 --> 00:00:38.496
In the first, the question is:

16
00:00:38.496 --> 00:00:40.768
will I spend money by accident?

17
00:00:40.768 --> 00:00:41.794
In the second:

18
00:00:41.794 --> 00:00:44.285
how do I put a site online safely?

19
00:00:44.285 --> 00:00:45.237
In the third:

20
00:00:45.237 --> 00:00:47.142
what does this error mean?

21
00:00:47.142 --> 00:00:50.952
Start with the one that answers your question today.

22
00:00:51.967 --> 00:00:55.153
And you don't need an AWS account to start.

23
00:00:55.153 --> 00:00:58.785
The first steps of every mission run without one.

24
00:00:58.785 --> 00:01:04.862
With one command, you can already check a sample cost report, with fictional data.

25
00:01:04.862 --> 00:01:11.013
If you move to AWS later, every mission shows you how to clean up what you created.

26
00:01:12.033 --> 00:01:13.667
There's just one rule.

27
00:01:13.667 --> 00:01:14.856
AI is the tutor.

28
00:01:14.856 --> 00:01:17.827
It asks questions, reviews and explains.

29
00:01:17.827 --> 00:01:22.654
But it makes mistakes, and catching them is part of the exercise.

30
00:01:22.654 --> 00:01:27.482
So check the numbers, open the links and write in your own words.

31
00:01:27.482 --> 00:01:28.596
Shall we start?

32
00:01:29.600 --> 00:01:31.515
One note before we finish.

33
00:01:31.515 --> 00:01:37.628
The voice you just heard was generated from my cloned voice, with my authorization.

34
00:01:37.628 --> 00:01:40.205
And this is an independent project.

35
00:01:40.205 --> 00:01:42.709
It is not official AWS material.
